# Build output. `target` is deliberately unanchored: the fuzz crate is built outside the
# workspace and has a `fuzz/target` of its own.
target
debug

# rustfmt backups
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC debugging information
*.pdb

# cargo-mutants
**/mutants.out*/

# cargo-fuzz working data. The targets are source and are committed; what they find is
# not — the corpus is machine-generated and unbounded, and a crash belongs in `tests/`
# with its input inlined.
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

# Coverage output, from a local `cargo llvm-cov`.
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info

# macOS
.DS_Store

# RustRover / IntelliJ
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md), anchored to the repository root.
# ROADMAP.md is the spec of specs: every open item names its feature specification.
#
# The upstream corpus — clones of s2-json, s2-connect and s2-documentation, the
# whitepaper, and the other implementations `cargo xtask interop` runs against — lives
# at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line. All of it is Apache-2.0 or CC-BY
# and re-cloned at will, indexed in `concepts/REFERENCES.md`; only the schemas are
# vendored, into schema/s2-json/. `xtask` reads it there, or from `$S2_REFERENCE`.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that produces
# them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, and
# the `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published tree
# may not cite a path its reader does not have; scripts/concepts-check.sh fails on one
# that does. Until 2026-11-13 `specs/` held the corpus now under `concepts/reference/`.
# Matching eebus, ocpp-kit, nuvec and speccoder.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/

# Zola build output
site/public/
